# Local secrets. `.env` holds live credentials for the example app and must never be committed;
# `.env.example` carries placeholders and IS committed. SEC-001 (#145) was a credential reaching a
# database column -- the same mistake in a git history is worse, because history is forever.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

